    "created_at": "2016-08-05T05:01:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-05T05:01:30Z",
    "body": "After some spec spelunking I think the correct course of action here to get silently-do-nothing semantics is to stop messing with the parser pause flag and instead use the ignore-destructive-writes counter. However, I have a separate proposal at https://github.com/w3c/webcomponents/issues/537 to instead throw. Implementing that would involve a separate counter (the \"throw-on-writes-and-closes counter\") which is only manipulated by the \"create an element for a token\" algorithm.\n",
